## Model card

- **Name:** GLM 4.7 Flash
- **Short description:** 30B-A3B MoE lightweight model with 1M context, MIT license, and balanced performance for agentic workflows; Z.ai's strongest model in the 30B class.
- **Provider / access:** Z.ai API Platform (`opencode/glm-4.7-flash`), Zen catalog; Chat Completions API.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2025 release; technical blog and model card available at arXiv 2508.06471 (Z.ai technical report).
- **IDs:** `opencode/glm-4.7-flash` (Zen), `zai-org/GLM-4.7-Flash` (Hugging Face, MIT)
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 total tokens (default 131,072 max new tokens, extensible; verified via Z.ai pricing and model card documentation).
- **Modalities:** Text in/out, reasoning support, tool calls, JSON mode, streaming, function calling.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-21):** Free on Zen (`$0 / $0` in/out, no cached read tier listed); Z.ai pricing page shows Free tier entry (GLM-4.7-Flash in "Text Models" section); data-usage/privacy caveats for free tiers: subject to Z.ai usage policies, rate limits, and possible data collection.
- **Architecture:** 30B-A3B MoE (1,024 active experts, 30B base + 1B active per token; MIT license), multi-turn agentic reasoning support (thinking mode, preserved thinking for multi-turn tasks), speculative decoding support, tool-call parser (glm47), reasoning parser (glm45).

